Interesting. I'd say the tidiest way for the game to deal with
situations like this would be for the game to shift the monster on the
upstairs up the stairs, making room for the player to land there. It
should always be the upstairs, no matter how the player entered the
level.

In the highly unlikely event the level above is already full, then the
game will have to shift *two* monsters up the stairs when the player
goes back up, to make room for the player and the monster we shifted
there earlier. (That monster needs to be found room on this level
rather than simply shunted up another level in case it is carrying the
amulet or something.)
If every level up to the top of the dungeon is full right then an
ever-expanding stack of monsters will be shunted up and up until they
reach the Dlvl1 stairs and get removed from the game, dumping their
inventories on the Dlvl1 upstair as they go.



